      "findingDispositions": [
        {
          "findingId": "B-3e16:F-008",
          "disposition": "verified_family",
          "familyKey": "forward-risk-resolveGraphPackage-asset-vendor-coupling",
          "reason": "Independently read packages/main/src/handlers/graph.ts resolveGraphPackage and describeLocation: assetDir and vendorDir are derived from packageRoot inside the same function that locates the dist/index.js entry, and startServer consumes both fields every invocation. Confirmed packages/graph/package.json has only main and types fields, no exports map, so no alternate seam exists today for asset/vendor path resolution once the entry-file import is deleted. Risk is real and specific to work not yet started; concurs with concept lane."
        },
        {
          "findingId": "B-3e16:F-009",
          "disposition": "verified_family",
          "familyKey": "forward-risk-file-dependency-precedent-unproven",
          "reason": "Independently confirmed: root package.json has no workspaces field; package-lock.json lockfileVersion 3 has zero entries for packages/main, packages/utils, or packages/graph as local packages. packages/main/node_modules/@lattice/lab is a manual symlink pointing to ../../../lab sitting inside gitignored node_modules, not reproduced by npm install, and grep confirms @lattice/lab is not statically imported anywhere in packages/main/src. Reverse case @proof-or-stop/core in packages/utils/package.json fails require.resolve. The cited precedent is genuinely unproven; concurs with quality lane."
        },
        {
          "findingId": "B-3e16:F-010",
          "disposition": "verified_family",
          "familyKey": "forward-risk-static-import-build-order-and-sqlite-hoist",
          "reason": "Independently confirmed both structural claims against current code: root package.json build script runs packages/main before packages/graph, so packages/graph/dist would not exist yet for a static import from main to resolve or type-check; and packages/graph/src/index.ts statically re-exports search from core/search/fn.js, which has a top-level import of DatabaseSync from node:sqlite -- a static import in handlers/graph.ts would hoist that load out of the current on-demand guarded path, since assertGraphRuntimeSupported runs strictly before the existing dynamic import per the load-bearing comment in graph.ts. Confirmed real regression risk in work not yet done; concurs with quality lane. Noted for the record and not part of this disposition: the user has since directed the fix to include splitting node:sqlite out of the eager re-export chain specifically to prevent this regression."
        },
        {
          "findingId": "B-3e16:F-011",
          "disposition": "verified_family",
          "familyKey": "doc-code-drift-complaint-count-off-by-one",
          "reason": "Independently reproduced from scratch in an isolated tmp copy of the full worktree, separate from the docs lane's own artifacts: positive control on unmodified process-fact-levels.ts passes cleanly with Process fact contract verified exit 0; after removing the graph entry and rerunning verify-process-fact-contract.mjs quiet, the failure output contains exactly nine distinct complaint lines, one MAIN_TOOLS missing from registry, seven DEFAULT_PHASE_TOOLS phase allowlist drift lines one per phase DEV DONE INIT INIT_CHECK PLAN REVIEW TEST, and one MAIN_TOOLS command missing from PROCESS_FACT_REGISTRY; restoring the entry returns to a clean pass. The decision doc text says eight. My own independent reproduction confirms nine, matching the docs lane; concurs with docs lane."
        },
        {
          "findingId": "B-3e16:F-012",
          "disposition": "verified_family",
          "familyKey": "doc-code-drift-unwired-contract-tasks",
          "reason": "Independently inspected proof-or-stop.config.json validate.commands, 113 entries with no match for surface or ownership as bare npm-script invocations, and root package.json test:serial-reference: cli-surface-smoke and verify-orphan-surface are absent from both, existing only as standalone npm run scripts. By contrast confirmed command-ownership-contract IS transitively covered: red-evidence-target-binding-smoke.ts, which is in validate.commands, internally invokes command-ownership-contract.js as a sub-check. This story's own CHK-003 verification evidence had to invoke test:orphan-surface manually, corroborating that nothing re-runs it automatically. Concurs with docs lane."
        },
        {
          "findingId": "B-3e16:F-013",
          "disposition": "verified_family",
          "familyKey": "forward-risk-advisory-stale-runtime-resolution-docs",
          "reason": "Independently confirmed both cited passages currently exist verbatim as described: packages/graph/README.md How the CLI reaches this package section states the handler resolves the package at RUNTIME rather than importing it statically because packages/graph is not a dependency of packages/main; packages/main/src/handlers/graph.ts MODULE RESOLUTION header comment gives the same rationale. Both would become false once the package becomes a file dependency with a static import, per the user's stated fix direction. Correctly scoped as advisory forward-risk, not a defect in the current merged tree; concurs with docs lane."
        }
      ],
